participating-org.narrative:
LDPA’s Vision: Persons with all types and levels of disability in Lao PDR  fully enjoy their rights and dignity.

LDPA’s Core Strategic Goals:
1. Persons with all types and levels of disability benefit from greater opportunities and participation, access to healthcare, education, employment, livelihoods and information at both the central and community levels;
2. Government, NPAs, OPDs and the private sector are better aware of and understand the rights of persons with disabilities;
3. LDPA Head Office and provincial Branch Offices have stronger organizational capacity and leadership and are able to effectively represent persons with all types and levels of disability.
LDPA is recognized by the Government, OPDs and many other stakeholders as a knowledgeable and skilled partner in the area of disability inclusion in Lao PDR. LDPA has close relationships with the NCDE Secretariat, and is an active member of the NCDE. In addition, LDPA facilitates the work of the DPO Executive Board, consisting of allOPDs and DSCs in the country.
